@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.12
@changelog
  - Codename: Bizarre Gardening Accident
  - UC1 gets full REC + RME (TotalReaper) integration on its focused-track surface. Encoder 2 rotation steps preamp gain +/-1 dB; Fine (or keyboard Shift) + rotation cycles the track's hardware input channel. Out of the box: 48V on Enc2 Push, Pad on Cut, Phase Invert on Polarity (all reassignable in Settings -> Modes -> REC). CS readout zone shows live "48V Pd Ph + gain" while in REC mode; brief flash to channel name on input-channel changes.
  - Fine button is momentary while REC / RecMon is the selection mode (was toggle); doubles as the Shift modifier for the Enc2 input-channel cycle. No more "Fine On / Off" readout flash in REC.
  - CS-scroll channel-name carousel suppressed entirely in REC + RME so the live preamp readout keeps updating during Encoder 1 channel changes. Carousel timeout elsewhere drops from 3 s to 1 s.
  - Nav Mode is rebuilt as a per-surface matrix (UF8 + UC1 each pick Regions or Markers independently; UC1 additionally has "Mirror UF8" = v0.1.11 behaviour, default). When one surface is in Regions and the other in Markers, the Markers surface auto-scopes to the Regions surface's currently-selected region — cursor move on one snaps the other to the first marker of the new scope.
  - UF8 region-press drill is suppressed when UC1 is in an independent Mode (would break the cross-coupling); jump still fires.
  - Settings -> Modes -> NAV is reorganised as a UF8 / UC1 column matrix. Legacy 4-state "Default view on entry" radio removed (UF8 Mode picker now is both entry default + live state). Push-action picker correctly labelled as shared between UC1 Encoder 2 and the UF8 Channel encoder.
